# wsg settings. Copy to ~/.config/wsg/config and adjust to taste.

# Where workspaces are created.
WS_ROOT="$HOME/workspaces"

# Command that launches the agent. `wsg new` starts it in the new workspace with /wsg-setup
# (unset: claude, if it is on PATH). `ws <slug>` uses it too; if unset, ws asks on first run and
# writes it here; `ws --agent` asks again. claude resumes the workspace's previous session, codex gets
# --add-dir for attached directories; any other command is run as-is.
# WSG_AGENT="claude"

# Language of CLI messages and ws: en or ru. If unset, taken from the locale (LC_ALL,
# LC_MESSAGES, LANG). Workspace files are always English. ws picks up a change in a new terminal;
# setting it here is more reliable than a LANG exported later in .zshrc.
# WSG_LANG="ru"

# Tracker prefix: if the ticket (wsg new --ticket, or the setup dialogue) is just a key or number,
# the link is built as "$WSG_TRACKER_URL$TICKET".
# WSG_TRACKER_URL="https://your-tracker.example.com/browse/"

# Your personal file of rules for working with the agent (how to review, what not to do without asking).
# If set, the workspace's AGENTS.md gets a section for a digest of it, filled during setup:
# Codex has its own file chain, and this file isn't part of it.
# WSG_GLOBAL_MEMORY="$HOME/.config/agent-rules.md"

# Context file one level above the workspaces that the agent loads in every session.
# Only counted toward the always-on budget in `wsg check`.
# WSG_PARENT_CONTEXT="$HOME/CLAUDE.md"
